        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "It genuinely makes me sad and angry to see players’ kindness being exploited for profit. They thought they were signing things for fans who genuinely support them, while some people only saw their kindness as a way to make money — even charging others just to see the photos. Real fans don’t need anything that comes at the cost of violating players’ privacy or boundaries. If this keeps happening, eventually genuine fans may lose these opportunities too. Please respect their boundaries, and to all the players: please protect your privacy and stay safe. They thought you were fans. You saw them as a business opportunity. That’s what makes this so disgusting."
        },
